<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Holocaust</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1941–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as The Holocaust, Shoah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Holocaust was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> of about six million European <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> by Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and its collaborators during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. From 1941 mass shootings in the occupied Soviet territories and the Baltic states were followed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportations</a> to extermination camps such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auschwitz-concentration-camp">Auschwitz-Birkenau</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treblinka-extermination-camp">Treblinka</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romani-people">Roma</a>, disabled people and other groups were also murdered on a mass scale.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/holocaust.jpg" alt="Holocaust" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernhard Walter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Selection_on_the_ramp_at_Auschwitz-Birkenau,_1944_(Auschwitz_Album)_1b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
